jobs.description:
Are you ready to apply your accounting skills in a challenging role within a growing and international environment? Do you enjoy ensuring financial records are accurate, compliant, and impeccably organized? 

We are looking for a Junior Accountant to join the finance team for a company in Leuven.

Your responsibilities will include:

AP accounting

• Register incoming invoices according to Belgian accounting and VAT principles and get them through
the approval cycle;

• Payments of suppliers and reconciliation of outgoing payments;

• Review and register expense notes.

General accounting

• Book and reconcile bank statements;

• Register journal entries;

• Register payroll bookings;

• Register fixed assets and book depreciations;

• Register prepaid expenses and provisions;

• Filing Belgian VAT returns;

• Register prepaid expenses and provisions.

• Bachelor in a relevant field (Finance, Accountancy) or assimilated by experience.

• Excellent knowledge of English and good knowledge of Dutch (spoken & written).

• Great attention to detail and good with numbers and figures and an analytical acumen.

• Good understanding of Belgian accounting and financial reporting principles and practices.

• Excellent knowledge of MS Office and familiarity with relevant computer software. Experience with NetSuite and/or Salesforce is a plus.

We are looking for a Business Process Engineer for our customer in Kortenberg

Main tasks and responsibilities:

This role fits in the implementation and introduction of a new ERP and other systms for providing services to our customers. Togetherwith the European team, you will be analyzing the existing processes and defining the best practices and contribute to a succesfull roll-out and maintenance of the new ERP system and other systems.

Investigating and Analyzing current business processes, procedures and requirements and mapping them to SharePoint;

Documenting visualization of process and procedure flows;

Identification and assessment of potential risks in business processes and development of risk mitigation strategies;

Re-engineering and optimization of business processes and shaping new process policies;

Proposing smarter process management solutions for performance improvement and cost reduction;

Illustrating project descriptions, objectives, and measurements;

Collaboration with various stakeholders to identify potential for improvement;

Participate in and hold meetings to perform incremental agile software development framework when managing product development;

Support to evaluate and test administrative system changes to provide ongoing support to existing applications and implement new applications;

Staying updated with new software features and industry trends and educating people in the group.
Profile:

Several years of experience in business process analysis and optimization;

Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;

Ability to critically question processes;

Excellent communication and teamwork skills;

Accuracy and care in the analysis and documentation of processes;

Language skills in English mandatory.

Professional skills:

Excellent knowledge of Business Process Modeling, Business Process Reengineering and the related Management (BPM) Tools;

SharePoint: Knowledge in using SharePoint for mapping business requirements and managing document workflows;

Data Analysis Tools: Skills in using tools like Excel or Power BI for analyzing business data and visualizing process flows;

Nice to have:

Knowledge in SAP S/4HANA public cloud;

Agile Frameworks: Understanding and applying agile methodologies for software development and project management;

Software Testing: Experience in professional software testing and quality assurance;

Experience in Project Management and related Software is an advantage: Experience with tools like JIRA, Trello, or Microsoft Project for managing tasks and tracking progress;

Programming Languages: A basic understanding of programming languages like Python, Java, or C# can be advantageous for accurately assessing the feasibility of proposed changes.
